# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Nature Spirit" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
0	section	Talking to Drezel
1	line	Player	Hello again, Drezel. Is there anything that I can help you out with around here?
1	cond	If the player does not meet the requirements for Nature Spirit:
2	line	Drezel	Well... I don't think so. There's not much to do in that place.
2	box	You do not meet all of the requirements to start the Nature Spirit quest.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player meets the requirements for Nature Spirit:
2	line	Drezel	Well... there is something you could do for me if you're interested. Though it is quite dangerous.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Well, what is it, I may be able to help?
3	line	Player	Well, what is it, I may be able to help?
3	line	Drezel	There's a man called Filliman who lives in Mort Myre. He comes by the temple from time to time but I haven't seen him recently. I was wondering if you could check in on him?
3	line	Drezel	I must warn you, it could be dangerous. Mort Myre is filled with ghasts!
3	select	Start Nature Spirit quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	Yes, I'll go and look for him.
4	line	Drezel	That's great! Many thanks!
4	line	Drezel	Now, please be aware of the ghasts, you cannot attack them, only Filliman knew how to take them on. Just run from them if you can. If you get lost, try to make your way back to the temple.
4	box	Drezel hands you some food.
4	line	Drezel	Please take this food to Filliman, he'll likely appreciate it. His home is somewhere in the southern end of Mort Myre. I don't know the exact location I'm afraid.
4	line	Player	Don't worry, if he's there and he's still alive, I'll find him.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Who exactly is this Filliman?
5	line	Player	Who exactly is this Filliman?
5	line	Drezel	Filliman Tarlock is his full name and he's a druid. He lives in Mort Myre much like a hermit, but there's many a traveller who he's helped.
5	line	Drezel	Most people that come this way tell stories of when they were lost and paths that just seemed to 'open up' before them! I think it was Filliman Tarlock helping out.
5	action	other
4	option	Where's Mort Myre?
5	line	Player	Where's Mort Myre?
5	line	Drezel	Mort Myre is a decayed and dangerous swamp to the south east of here. Legend says it was once a beautiful forest called Humblethorn. Now, it's filled with vile emanations from within Morytania.
5	line	Drezel	The swamp decays everything. We put a fence around it to stop unwary travellers going in. Anyone who dies in the swamp is forever cursed to haunt it as a ghast.
5	line	Drezel	Ghasts attack travellers, turning food to rotten filth.
5	action	other
4	option	What's a ghast?
5	line	Player	What's a ghast?
5	line	Drezel	A Ghast is a poor soul who died in Mort Myre. They're undead of a special class and they're untouchable as far as I'm aware! Filliman knows how to tackle them though.
5	line	Drezel	When they attack, ghasts will devour any food you have. If you have no food, they'll draw their nourishment from you!
5	action	other
4	option	I'd better get going.
5	line	Player	I'd better get going.
5	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	Sorry, I don't think I can help.
4	line	Drezel	That's fine, I'm sure someone else will be along shortly who can. Now, if you will excuse me, I do have some things to be getting on with.
4	action	end
2	option	Sorry, not interested.
3	line	Player	Sorry, not interested.
3	line	Drezel	Of course. I understand.
3	action	end
0	section	Talking to Drezel again
1	line	Player	Hello again!
1	line	Drezel	Have you managed to find Filliman yet?
1	line	Player	No not yet.
1	line	Drezel	Please go and look for him, I would appreciate it!
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Where should I look for Filliman Tarlock again?
2	line	Player	Where should I look for Filliman Tarlock again?
2	line	Drezel	Search to the south of Mort Myre. Remember that he's a druid so he can conceal himself within nature quite well. My guess is that he lives in the southern area of the swamp, though he could be anywhere.
2	action	initial
1	option	Explain to me what a Ghast is again.
2	line	Player	Explain to me what a Ghast is again.
2	line	Drezel	A Ghast is a poor soul who died in Mort Myre. They're undead of a special class, they're untouchable apart from with special druidic items.
2	line	Drezel	Filliman knew how to tackle them, but I've not heard from him in a long time. Ghasts, when they attack, will devour any food you have. If you have no food, they'll draw their nourishment from you!
2	action	initial
1	option	What's the story with Mort Myre?
2	line	Player	What's the story with Mort Myre?
2	line	Drezel	Mort Myre was once a beautiful forest by the name of Humblethorn until the evil denizens of Morytania descended. Now their evil emanations have putrified and diseased the forest into a decaying swamp of death.
2	action	initial
1	option	What's the story with Filliman Tarlock?
2	line	Player	What's the story with Filliman Tarlock?
2	line	Drezel	Filliman is a druid of some considerable power. He helped many people in Morytania escape when the evil descended upon the land. His knowledge of plants and nature was exceptional.
2	line	Drezel	But one day, he was betrayed by some of the people who he had tried to help. This naturally made him more careful when dealing with strangers again and so, instead of showing himself, he would follow them.
2	line	Drezel	He would follow them at a distance and make the path clear for them, showing them to the temple and to salvation. Saradomin bless him! He is a good man.
2	action	initial
1	option	Ok, thanks.
2	line	Player	Ok, thanks.
2	line	Drezel	Many thanks to you, {player}!
2	action	end
