0	section	Talking to Filliman
1	cond	If the player attempts to enter the Grotto:
2	box	A shifting apparition appears in front of you.
2	cond	If the player is not wearing the Ghostspeak amulet:
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Cannot wake up... Where am I?
3	line	Player	Huh? What's this?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	What did I write down now? Put it in the knot hole.
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Ahhrs Oooohh arhhhhAHhhh.
3	line	Player	Huh! Now you're just not making any sense at all! I just cannot understand you!
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player is wearing the Ghostspeak amulet:
3	line	Player	Hello?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Oh, I understand you! At last, someone who doesn't just mumble. I understand what you're saying!
3	select	Select an option
3	option	I'm wearing an amulet of ghost speak!
4	line	Player	I'm wearing an amulet of ghost speak!
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	Why you poor fellow, have you passed away and you want to send a message back to a loved one?
4	line	Player	Err.. Not exactly...
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	You have come to haunt my dreams until I pass on your message to a dearly loved one. I understand. Pray, tell me who would you like me to pass a message on to?
4	line	Player	Ermm, you don't understand... It's just that..
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	Yes!
4	line	Player	Well, please don't be upset or anything... But you're the ghost!
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	Don't be silly now! That in no way reflects the truth!
4	action	initial
3	option	How long have you been a ghost?
4	line	Player	How long have you been a ghost?
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	What?! Don't be preposterous! I'm not a ghost! How could you say something like that?
4	line	Player	But it's true, you're a ghost... well, at least that is to say, you're sort of not alive anymore.
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	Don't be silly, I can see you, I can see that tree. If I were dead, I wouldn't be able to see anything.. What you say just doesn't reflect the truth. You'll have to try harder to pull one over on me!
4	action	initial
3	option	What's it like being a ghost?
4	line	Player	What's it like being a ghost?
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	Oh, it's quite.... Oh... Trying to catch me out were you! Anyone can clearly see that I am not a ghost!
4	line	Player	But you are a ghost, look at yourself! I can see straight through you! You're as dead as this swamp! Err... No offence or anything...
4	line	Filliman Tarlock	No I won't take offence because I'm not dead and I'm afraid you'll have to come up with some pretty conclusive proof before I believe it. What a strange dream this is.
4	action	initial
3	option	Ok, thanks.
4	line	Player	Ok thanks.
4	action	end
0	section	Talking to Drezel after talking to Filliman without a ghostspeak amulet
1	line	Player	I've found Filliman and you should prepare for some sad news.
1	line	Drezel	You mean... he's dead?
1	line	Player	Well, er sort of. I got to his camp and I encountered a spirit of some kind. I don't think it was a Ghast, it tried to communicate with me, but made no sense, it was all 'ooooh' this and 'oooh' that.
1	line	Drezel	Hmmm, that's very interesting, I seem to remember Father Aereck in Lumbridge and his predecessor Father Urhney having a similar issue. Though this is probably not related to your problem.
1	line	Drezel	I will pray that it wasn't the spirit of my friend Filliman, but some lost soul who needs some help. Please do let me know how you get on with it.
1	action	end
0	section	Using the journal on Filliman before using the mirror
1	line	Filliman Tarlock	Oh, keep hold of that, I may need it later.
1	action	end
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with Filliman
1	cond	If the player talks to him again without wearing a ghostspeak amulet:
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	Ahhrs Oooohh arhhhhAHhhh.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player talks to him again after speaking to him with a ghostspeak amulet:
2	line	Player	Hello again!
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	Oh, hello there, do you still think I'm dead? It's hard to see how I could be dead when I'm still in the world. I can see everything quite clearly. And nothing of what you say reflects the truth.
2	line	Player	Yes, I do think you're dead and I'll prove it somehow.
2	action	initial
1	cond	If the player uses the mirror on Filliman without wearing the ghostspeak amulet:
2	action	above
1	cond	If the player uses the mirror on Filliman whilst wearing the ghostspeak amulet:
2	box	You use the mirror on the spirit of the dead Filliman Tarlock.
2	line	Player	Here take a look at this, perhaps you can see that you're utterly transparent now!
2	box	The spirit of Filliman reaches forwards and takes the mirror.
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	Well, that is the most peculiar thing I've ever experienced. This mirror must somehow be dysfunctional. Strange how well it reflects the stagnant swamp behind me, but there is nothing of my own
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	visage apparent.
2	line	Player	That's because you're dead! Dead as a door nail.. Deader in fact... You bear a remarkable resemblance to worm bait! Err.. No offence...
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	I think you might be right my friend, though I still feel very much alive. It is strange how I still come to be here and yet I've not turned into a Ghast.
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	It must be a sign... Yes a sign... I must try to find out what it means. Now, where did I put my journal?
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player uses his journal on Filliman without wearing the ghostspeak amulet:
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	Ahhrs Oooohh arhhhhAHhhh.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player uses his journal on Filliman whilst wearing the ghostspeak amulet:
2	box	You give the journal to Filliman Tarlock.
2	line	Player	Here, I found this, maybe you can use it?
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	My journal! That should help to collect my thoughts.
2	box	~ The spirit starts leafing through the journal. ~ ~ He seems quite distant as he regards the pages. ~ ~ After some time the druid faces you again. ~
2	line	Filliman Tarlock	It's all coming back to me now. It looks like I came to a violent and bitter end but that's not important now. I just have to figure out what I am going to do now?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Being dead, what options do you think you have?
3	line	Player	Being dead, what options do you think you have? I'm not trying to be rude or something, but it's not like you have many options is it? I mean, it's either up or down for you isn't it?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Hmm, well you're a poetic one aren't you. Your material world logic stands you in good stead... If you're standing in the material world...
3	action	initial
2	option	So, what's your plan?
3	line	Player	So, what's your plan?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	In my former incarnation I was Filliman Tarlock, a great druid of some power. I spent many years in this place, which was once a forest and I would wish to protect it as a nature sprit.
3	action	initial
2	option	Well, good luck with that.
3	line	Player	Well, good luck with that.
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Won't you help me to become a nature spirit? I could really use your help!
3	action	initial
2	option	How can I help?
3	line	Player	How can I help?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Will you help me to become a nature spirit? The directions for becoming one are a bit vague, I need three things but I know how to get one of them. Perhaps you can help collect the rest?
3	line	Player	I might be interested, what's involved?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Well, the book says, that I need, and I quote:- 'Something with faith', 'something from nature' and 'something of the 'spirit-to-become' freely given'. Hmm, I know how to get something from nature.
3	line	Player	Well, that does seem a bit vague.
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	Hmm, it does and I could understand if you didn't want to help. However, if you could perhaps at least get the item from nature, that would be a start. Perhaps we can figure out the rest as we go along.
3	box	The druid produces a small sheet of papyrus with some writing on it.
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	This spell needs to be cast in the swamp after you have been blessed. I'm afraid you'll need to go to the temple to the North and ask a member of the clergy to bless you.
3	line	Player	Blessed, what does that do?
3	line	Filliman Tarlock	It is required if you're to cast this druid spell. Once you've cast the spell, you should find something from nature. Bring it back to me and then we'll try to figure out the other things we need.
3	action	end
2	option	Ok thanks.
3	line	Player	Ok thanks.
3	action	end
